frontlet_data:alpes_Person_201 a frontlet:Person ;
    frontlet:aged [ a frontlet:Age ;
            frontlet:hasAge 46 ] ;
    frontlet:birthPlace frontlet_data:alpes_Country_SYR ;
    frontlet:composedOf frontlet_data:alpes_Death_gen_201 ;
    frontlet:gender thes:male ;
    frontlet:hasComment """Selon les infos reportées dans le journal: "S PU Murska Sobota so sporoÄili, da so 13. novembra med postopkom evidentiranja tujcev v sprejemnem centru PetiÅ¡ovci ugotovili, da je zdravstveno stanje 46-letnega drÅ¾avljana Sirije zelo slabo. Odpeljali so ga v RakiÄan, tam je Å¡e isti dan umrl zaradi odpovedi notranjih organov. Preden je izdihnil, je povedal, da je med prebijanjem v EU Å¾e moral poiskati zdravniÅ¡ko pomoÄ v TurÄiji. Strokovni direktor rakiÄanske bolniÅ¡nice Danijel Grabar pravi, da Sircu res ni bilo pomoÄi. Â»Å½e zdavnaj bi se moral zdraviti, tako pa je rakavo obolenje pri njem napredovalo do te mere, da so mu ob sprejemu Å¾e mnoÅ¾iÄno odpovedovali organi.Â«"
"PU Murska Sobota announced that on November 13, during the process of registering foreigners at the PetiÅ¡ovci screening center, they found that the health condition of a 46-year-old citizen of Syria was very poor. They took him to RakiÄan, where he died the same day due to internal organ failure. Before he breathed his last, he said that while he was being beaten in the EU, he had to seek medical help in Turkey. Danijel Grabar, the professional director of the hospital in Rakica, says that Sirca was really not helped. "He should have been cured a long time ago, so his cancer progressed to such an extent that his organs failed en masse."\"""" .

